  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA multiprofile with scvi_n200 and transformer aggregation is the best setting, outperforming PCA and single-profile baselines. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the untested scgpt RNA encoder can improve on scvi_n200 under this same strong profile/aggregation setting. config_009 changes only the RNA encoder relative to the current best, isolating representation quality. This is a clean exploitation of the most promising direction and is more informative than jumping to multimodal fusion, which would change several factors at once."
